# Reuse Existing UI Components

When building or editing UI, use shared components from `components/Atoms` and `components/Molecules` instead of raw HTML controls with one-off styles.

## Prefer these first

| Need | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Dropdown / `<select>` | `@/components/Atoms/Select` |
| Text / number / date inputs | `@/components/Atoms/Input` |
| Buttons | `@/components/Atoms/Button` |
| Radio groups | `@/components/Atoms/RadioSelect` |
| Search fields | `@/components/Molecules/SearchInput` (or existing search patterns) |

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — native select with ad-hoc classes
<select
  value={season}
  onChange={e => setSeason(e.target.value)}
  className="mt-1 w-full bg-black/30 border border-noir-gold/30 rounded px-3 py-2"
>
  {options.map(o => (
    <option key={o.id} value={o.id}>{o.label}</option>
  ))}
</select>

// ✅ GOOD — shared Select atom
<Select
  selectId="wear-journal-season"
  label={t("season")}
  selectData={options}
  value={season}
  action={e => setSeason(e.target.value)}
  className="w-full max-w-none md:w-full"
/>
```

## Guidelines

- Before adding a new control, check `components/Atoms` and nearby feature usage for an existing pattern
- Match props used elsewhere (`selectData` with `{ id, name, label }`, `action` + `value` for controlled selects)
- Do not invent a parallel styled `<select>`, `<button>`, or `<input>` when an atom already exists
- Only use a raw element when no shared component covers the need (e.g. `textarea` if there is no Textarea atom yet) — keep styling aligned with existing atoms when possible
- If a shared component is missing a needed variant, extend that component rather than forking styles in the page
